      "description": "Busy is the share of each second a task spends doing work; back-pressured is the share it spends blocked because the task downstream of it cannot keep up. Busy near 100% with no back-pressure means the pipeline is working at its limit and keeping up. Sustained back-pressure means it is not: the offered load is above what this parallelism can absorb, and adding parallelism is what fixes it.",
